# Git for Windows checks LF out as CRLF by default (core.autocrlf=true). That
# breaks scripts/lib/i18n-block.js, whose pattern joins its five lines with a
# bare \n, so `npm run build:prod` fails before compiling anything (#142).
# Pin the working tree to LF on every platform instead of depending on each
# contributor's own setting.
* text=auto eol=lf

# text=auto detects these already; spelled out so a diff or a merge driver
# never treats one as text on a misconfigured client.
*.png  binary
*.gif  binary
*.jpg  binary
*.ico  binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
